gputest.c and gpu.c adapt the triangle setup and command encoding to native
Plan 9 C, gpu(3), libdraw and libmemdraw. The Red Hat copyright and MIT permission
notice are preserved in LICENSE. No renderer, Mesa, TGSI compiler or Linux
driver is linked into the guest. TGSI text is compiled by host VirGL.
The device tests and generated9 integration use the root LICENSE.

VirtIO GPU transport

Specification: OASIS VirtIO 1.2, section 5.7 (GPU Device)
https://docs.oasis-open.org/virtio/virtio/v1.2/virtio-v1.2.html

Wire layouts were also checked against include/uapi/linux/virtio_gpu.h,
Linux v6.12, revision adc218676eef25575469234709c2d87185ca223a:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/adc218676eef25575469234709c2d87185ca223a/include/uapi/linux/virtio_gpu.h
Its Red Hat copyright, Dave Airlie and Gerd Hoffmann attribution, and BSD
permission notice are preserved in sys/src/9/pc/devgpu.c.
The driver reuses 9front's existing virtio10pc register access and follows
the PCI capability and split queue conventions of sdvirtio10.c.

Utah teapot

Source: https://github.com/freeglut/freeglut
Revision: 69ac8824f003dd813ceb14b11fb4efaa38cb4aa9
Files: src/fg_teapot_data.h and src/fg_teapot.c

teapot.h contains the ten input patches and 129 control points, with
native C types and local names. The remaining teaset data is omitted.
Martin Newell created the teapot; the source credits Philip Schneider and
Juhana Kouhia for the archived data. Freeglut reduces symmetric patches
and adds the bottom. Its original permission notice is retained.
mesh.c adapts the Bernstein patch evaluation, normals and symmetry to
an indexed native mesh, with the original Pawel W. Olszta MIT notice.
The shaders, animation and native window integration use the root LICENSE.
No GLUT or OpenGL client library is linked into the guest.

VirGL v1 capabilities were checked against src/vrend_renderer.c at the
virglrenderer revision above: depth formats are advertised in sampler,
and vertexbuffer lists optional formats, not baseline float vertices.
